      },
      "knownGap": {
        "what": "the optimal split of the plane change between the two burns",
        "why": "computeCombinedManeuver takes the ENTIRE inclination change at burn 2. That is the textbook's FIRST answer, not its final one: splitting a small part of the turn into the departure burn is cheaper, and the saving here is 24.65 m/s (0.58%) on a single transfer. This row is an EXPECTED FAILURE that documents the unimplemented optimisation. It must never pass silently — if the module ever starts returning the optimal figure, this row FAILS and forces a deliberate re-baseline."
